11-Why is automated testing important in DevOps?

It is important because testing repeates regularly, so it´s easier to identify the issues and deal with it quickly.

12-What is configuration drift, and how can it be reduced?

Configuration drift is the gradual and often unintended divergence of a system´s actual settings from its intended baseline state over time.
It can be reduced by adopting IaC using tools like terraform.

13- Why are small and frequent deployments considered a DevOps best practice?

Because they make software delivery safer, faster, and easier to manage.
For example, each deployment contains fewer changes, so automated tests can more easily identify problems.

14- What are the main steps for responding to a failed deployment?

Detect → Assess → Stop → Roll back → Investigate → Fix → Test → Redeploy → Learn.

15- How can Git, Jenkins, Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, Ansible, Prometheus, and Grafana work together?

1. Git (and Github) - Manages Codes and Documents with Branching, Merging, Push/Pull, Repository...
2. Jenkins - Automates activities such as building, testing, and deploying software
3. Docker and Kubernetes - Creates portable containers which contains products from previous steps and manage them
4. Terraform - Defines and provisions infrastructure using configuration files
5. Ansible - Automates server configuration, application deployment, and repetitive operational tasks
6. Prometheus - Collects time-series metrics and supports monitoring and alerts of the final product
7. Grafana - Displays metrics and other monitoring data through dashboards so that operations team can visually identify the issues more easily.
